 Fine-tuning scripts generally take a pre-trained checkpoint, a tokenizer, and a model config, and select the model class via `--model_cls` (for example, `src.gena_lm.modeling_bert:BertForSequenceClassification` or the RMT classes in `src.gena_lm.modeling_rmt`).
 
 ## Example notebooks
 
-- `notebooks/GENA_sequence_classification_example.ipynb` — fine-tunes a pre-trained GENA-LM model on the promoter prediction task as sequence classification ([Open in Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)).
+- `notebooks/GENA_sequence_classification_example.ipynb` — fine-tunes a pre-trained GENA-LM model on the promoter prediction task as sequence classification ([Open in Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/github/AIRI-Institute/GENA_LM/blob/main/notebooks/GENA_sequence_classification_example.ipynb)).
 - `notebooks/gena_enformer_usage.ipynb` — uses the GENA-LM model fine-tuned on the Enformer dataset (loaded with `revision='enformer'`) to find mutations linked to a gene.
 - `notebooks/gena_clusterization_example.ipynb` — clusters DNA sequences using GENA-LM embeddings.
 - `notebooks/public_gena_clusters.ipynb` and `notebooks/public_gena_clusters_task.ipynb` — differentiate species (from yeast and bacteria to mammals) by embedding DNA chunks with GENA-LM and visualizing them with t-SNE/UMAP.
 - `notebooks/HSE.task3.table_full.csv` and `notebooks/HSE.task3.table_sample.csv` — variant tables (`pos`, `ref`, `alt`) accompanying the clustering task; `2023-08-10 19_40_52.828317species_extended_metadata.csv` contains species assembly metadata.

